{
 "about": "One-line breaks of the betting set, each with the one test that goes red. For each: apply its edits to the file (each find occurs exactly once in the file as committed; a find of several lines is one anchor), run the named test alone and see it fail, restore the file byte for byte and see it pass. Forge matches --match-test against the test's name with its parentheses, so the pattern below ends in an escaped parenthesis. Check that exactly one test ran. Ids: B, the cut's: the (home, away) order, the settlement's status read, the fill path, the registry and the interface pins.",
